---
import Layout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Remembering Bonnie Durocher/Sutton | William64.com"
  description="Remembering Bonnie Durocher/Sutton, a caring mother, and supporting William and Eric as they honor her life."
>
  <header class="page-header memorial-header split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">In loving memory</p><h1>
        Bonnie Durocher/<wbr />Sutton
      </h1><p class="lede">
        A place to remember Bonnie, to share the love her family carries for
        her, and to help William and Eric honor her life with dignity.
      </p><div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://gofund.me/bc6e369e2"
          >Support the family ↗</a
        ><a class="btn" href="#story">Read her story ↓</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="memorial-portrait">
      <img
        src="/images/bonnie-memorial.jpg"
        alt="A treasured family photograph shared for Bonnie's memorial"
        width="1200"
        height="900"
      /><figcaption>
        A treasured photograph shared by Bonnie’s family.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </header>
  <div class="split" id="story">
    <article class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Her story</p><h2>
        Remembering a hardworking, caring mother.
      </h2>
      <p>
        William and Eric Sutton are organizing this fundraiser in memory of
        their mother, <strong>Bonnie Durocher/Sutton</strong>, during an
        incredibly painful time. Bonnie recently passed away, leaving a deep
        void in the lives of everyone who loved her.
      </p>
      <p>
        She was a hardworking, caring woman who spent <strong
          >35 years at Square D</strong
        >, where she was well known and respected, and where she later retired.
        Bonnie put others before herself and worked tirelessly to provide for
        her family.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the past several years, William and Eric devoted their own time,
        energy, and resources to helping care for her. Now, while grieving, they
        are also carrying the financial burden of her cremation and final
        expenses, which can easily exceed $3,000.
      </p>
      <p>
        The family hopes to give Bonnie the memorial she deserves: a meaningful
        celebration of life that honors her with dignity and love. If giving is
        not possible, sharing this page and keeping William, Eric, and their
        family in your thoughts and prayers would mean so much.
      </p>
      <p>
        With sincere gratitude,<br /><strong>William and Eric Sutton</strong>
      </p>
    </article>
    <aside class="card memorial-support sticky-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Help honor Bonnie</p><h2>
        Give, share, or remember.
      </h2><p>
        Every contribution helps ease the pressure on Bonnie’s children and
        supports her cremation, final expenses, and celebration of life.
      </p><div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://gofund.me/bc6e369e2"
          >Open the GoFundMe ↗</a
        >
      </div><hr /><p class="small">
        Donations are handled securely by GoFundMe. This page does not collect
        payment information.
      </p><p class="small">
        Campaign created August 31, 2026. The original campaign showed 0 donors
        at launch; visit GoFundMe for current information.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
